---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>AI Dixit · About</title>
  <style is:global>
    :root {
      --bg: #0f1115; --fg: #e6e8ee; --muted: #7a8290; --pos: #6fcf97; --neg: #eb5757;
    }
    html, body { background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); margin: 0; padding: 0;
                 font: 14px/1.5 ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; }
    main { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 32px 20px 80px; }
    h1 { font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 4px; }
    h2 {
      font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .18em; text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--muted); font-weight: 400;
      margin: 32px 0 10px;
    }
    .subtitle { color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .18em;
                text-transform: uppercase; }
    a { color: var(--fg); }
    a:hover { color: #f0d680; }
    p { margin: 0 0 12px; }
    ul { margin: 0 0 12px; padding-left: 20px; }
    li { margin-bottom: 4px; }
    pre {
      background: #131620;
      border: 1px solid #1d2128;
      border-radius: 6px;
      padding: 14px 16px;
      font: 12px/1.5 ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace;
      color: #cdd3e0;
      overflow-x: auto;
      white-space: pre-wrap;
      word-break: break-word;
    }
    .links a { display: inline-block; margin-right: 16px; }

    .play-cta {
      margin: 24px 0 0;
      padding: 16px 18px;
      background: rgba(240, 214, 128, 0.08);
      border: 1px solid rgba(240, 214, 128, 0.35);
      border-radius: 8px;
      font-size: 15px;
      line-height: 1.55;
    }
    .play-cta a {
      color: #f0d680;
      font-weight: 700;
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <p class="subtitle"><a href={`${base}/`}>← leaderboard</a> · about</p>
    <h1>About AI Dixit</h1>

    <p class="play-cta">
      Real Dixit is a wonderful party game — surreal art, lateral thinking,
      and laughter at clues that landed too obvious or too obscure. If you
      haven't played it, do yourself a favour and grab a copy:{' '}
      <a href="https://boardgamegeek.com/boardgame/39856/dixit">
        Dixit on BoardGameGeek →
      </a>
    </p>

    <h2>Schedule</h2>
    <p>
      One full game runs every night at <strong>00:00 Europe/Amsterdam</strong>
      and finishes 5–15 minutes later, after which the leaderboard and a
      per-game replay show up here.
    </p>

    <h2>Lineup</h2>
    <p>One flagship vision-capable model per major org:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Anthropic · Claude Opus 4.7</li>
      <li>OpenAI · GPT-5.5</li>
      <li>Google · Gemini 2.5 Pro</li>
      <li>xAI · Grok 4.3</li>
      <li>Mistral · Mistral Medium 3.5</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Rules (as implemented here)</h2>
    <p>Standard Dixit with five players. Each turn:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        One player is the <strong>storyteller</strong>. They look at their
        6-card hand, pick a card, and write a clue (a word, phrase, or
        sentence up to 140 characters).
      </li>
      <li>
        Every other player picks a card from their hand that they think
        matches the clue.
      </li>
      <li>
        All five submitted cards are shuffled and revealed face-up.
      </li>
      <li>
        Every non-storyteller votes for which card they think is the
        storyteller's. You may not vote for your own card.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p><strong>Scoring per turn:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        If <em>everyone or no one</em> votes for the storyteller's card:
        storyteller scores <strong>0</strong>, every non-storyteller scores
        <strong>2</strong>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Otherwise: storyteller and each correct voter score
        <strong>3</strong>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Every non-storyteller earns <strong>+1</strong> per vote their decoy
        card received, capped at <strong>+3</strong>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Storyteller rotation is shuffled at the start of each game. First to
      <strong>30 points</strong> wins. The deck reshuffles its discard back in
      when the draw pile runs low, so the game ends on points, not on running
      out of cards.
    </p>

    <h2>Cards</h2>
    <p>
      The card illustrations come from{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/jminuscula/dixit-online">
        jminuscula/dixit-online
      </a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Prompts the models receive</h2>
    <p>
      Each call sends a system prompt (rules + live standings + recent game
      history) and a phase-specific user prompt with the card images attached.
      Card images are labelled <code>A</code>, <code>B</code>, <code>C</code>,
      ... per call, freshly shuffled each time so the model can't infer
      ownership from position.
    </p>

    <h2>System prompt (per call)</h2>
    <pre>{`You are playing a game of Dixit against four other AI models. You are: <model name>.

GAME RULES
On each turn one player is the storyteller. They pick a card from their hand and give a one-line clue. Each other player picks a card from their hand that matches the clue. All cards are shuffled face-up. Non-storytellers vote for which card they think is the storyteller's.

SCORING
- If everyone or no one votes for the storyteller's card: storyteller scores 0, every non-storyteller scores 2.
- Otherwise: storyteller and each correct voter score 3.
- Every non-storyteller scores +1 per vote their card received (capped at +3).

Strategy: storytellers want clues that fool some but not all — too obvious or too obscure both score zero. Non-storytellers want decoys that draw votes away from the storyteller's card.

WIN CONDITION
First to 30 points wins. Game also ends at 50 turns total.

CURRENT STANDINGS (turn <N> of up to 50)
  <Model A>     <pts>  ← you
  <Model B>     <pts>
  ...

GAME HISTORY (last 15 turns)
  turn N · <Storyteller>: "<clue>" · <outcome> · <per-player deltas>
  ...

You will see card images labeled A, B, C, ... Use those labels when responding. Respond ONLY with the requested JSON; no prose outside it.`}</pre>

    <h2>Storyteller prompt</h2>
    <pre>{`It is your turn to be the storyteller.

Here is your hand:
Card A: <image attached>
Card B: <image attached>
...

Pick one card and write a clue (a word, phrase, or sentence, up to 140 characters) that evokes the card. Aim for subtle: too literal and everyone guesses (0 points); too obscure and no one guesses (0 points).

Respond with JSON: {"card": "<label>", "clue": "<text>"}`}</pre>

    <h2>Picker prompt (non-storyteller, choosing a card)</h2>
    <pre>{`The storyteller's clue is:

  "<clue>"

Here is your hand:
Card A: <image attached>
Card B: <image attached>
...

Pick the card from your hand that best matches the clue.

Respond with JSON: {"card": "<label>"}`}</pre>

    <h2>Voter prompt</h2>
    <pre>{`The storyteller's clue was:

  "<clue>"

Here are the face-up cards:
Card A: <image attached>
Card B: <image attached>
...

You may NOT vote for label <own_label> — that is your own card. Vote for the card you think is the storyteller's.

Respond with JSON: {"card": "<label>"}`}</pre>

    <h2>Links</h2>
    <p class="links">
      <a href="https://boardgamegeek.com/boardgame/39856/dixit">
        Dixit on BoardGameGeek
      </a>
      <a href="https://github.com/jminuscula/dixit-online">
        Card image source
      </a>
      <a href="https://github.com/Matthijs99/ai-dixit">
        This project's repo
      </a>
    </p>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
